\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Comparing averages on nested partitions}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{A Fourier coefficient samples the whole periodic grid. An
average over adjacent sites instead records a local part of the
field, as in the circle calculation of \ref{fdip-00G1}.
For a periodic grid in higher dimension, equal coordinate
subregions provide the analogous observations. How should the
averaging maps be normalized, and how should observations on a
finer partition be combined to match a coarser one?}
